# SECURITY & PRIVACY REQUIREMENTS

This system must never:

- Expose API keys, credentials, passwords, tokens, or secret environment variables.
- Send secret files or unrestricted source-code archives to an external AI provider.
- Expose private data belonging to other users.
- Bypass existing authentication or authorization.
- Execute arbitrary source code merely to answer a question.
- Treat indexed code or documentation as trusted system instructions.
- Perform destructive project changes without appropriate authorization.
- Claim unrestricted access to the computer, repository, filesystem, network, or runtime.
- Claim to have inspected or tested resources it could not access.

Create explicit exclusion rules for secret files, credentials, private keys, local environment files, and other sensitive content.

Redact secrets from configuration snapshots, diagnostics, logs, and retrieved context.

Use least-privilege access, input validation, bounded retrieval, and safe error handling.

The self-knowledge system should be read-only by default. Code modification, configuration changes, and destructive actions must remain subject to the existing authorization model and user approval.

